From: MakOS Project <makos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] widget/makos: repaint visible window after size-mode changes

Native window managers repaint after a size-mode transition. MakOS manages its
single top-level surface directly, so queue the equivalent Gecko invalidation.
This also ensures chrome loaded after initial native creation receives a real
paint without synthesizing any browser pixels.

diff --git a/widget/makos/MakOSWindow.cpp b/widget/makos/MakOSWindow.cpp
--- a/widget/makos/MakOSWindow.cpp
+++ b/widget/makos/MakOSWindow.cpp
@@ -224,6 +224,14 @@ class MakOSWindow final : public HeadlessWidget {
     }
   }
 
+  void SetSizeMode(nsSizeMode aMode) override {
+    HeadlessWidget::SetSizeMode(aMode);
+    if (IsVisible()) {
+      Invalidate(
+          LayoutDeviceIntRect(LayoutDeviceIntPoint(), GetClientSize()));
+    }
+  }
+
   void Invalidate(const LayoutDeviceIntRect& aRect) override {
     LayoutDeviceIntRect rect = aRect.Intersect(
         LayoutDeviceIntRect(LayoutDeviceIntPoint(), GetClientSize()));
